-- and the same class pair with the exchange made fast, which is one signal. What makes it fast is not the
-- temperature -- heating the solution to 90 C leaves the anomers resolved -- but a catalyst, base or
-- glucose isomerase, which is in the medium. So this case says the rate belongs to the condition and not
-- only to the molecule, and the setting as it stands carries the temperature, the resolving rate and the
-- handedness but not what else is dissolved. That is the next thing the setting has to hold, and the
-- reason it has to hold it is a sugar in water.
glu-catalysed : Compound
glu-catalysed = (2 , cons (nat-xch (cons 0 nil) (cons 1 nil) , rate-flat 3 , true) nil , cons 0 (cons 1 nil))
